{"id": "EUVD-2026-82280", "enisaUuid": "963558fb-d45a-3b4a-8537-0adb87a32c6e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/mm_init: handle alloc_percpu failure in free_area_init_core_hotplug\n\nWe miss a failed allocation check for pgdat->per_cpu_nodestats, which\nresults in a NULL deref when we offset into the per-cpu area.\n\nPropagate -ENOMEM up the stack and leave per_cpu_nodestats pointing\nat boot_nodestats so a later online can retry the allocation.\n\nhotadd_init_pgdat() returns NULL on failure, which __try_online_node()\nalready maps to -ENOMEM.\n\nOn failure nothing needs to be unwound:\n  - the node is never marked online\n  - per_cpu_nodestats is left pointing at boot_nodestats\n  - __add_memory_resource() cleans up pending memblock resources\n  - later online attempts retry the per_cpu_nodestats allocation", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dda09e7ca0bf0c3fa7c5c8f134d9804b67f455c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cc5caef9a8d1894dfa31d84a0daa0ac1437dadc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc3b5e6519b8df22d622a03eab6772784da97db4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1017fe1c7f48e511c5a680e3057005daaff2f3a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ebce860bdd7ae5e13002811bc9bbbf33fcfc221"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93172", "GHSA-3775-xr2m-86hx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "014320a5-04d8-3120-bb47-815ecfe2d571", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "06b9edae-eae7-3ae7-a829-a7ba21499710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0a58283f-3abe-3d6c-98a7-ff54ea4dc545", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "33ebc404-b8ab-3da3-b889-09fd6e272459", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, 